1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,622
Most genes on the X chromosome have no partner on the much smaller Y.

2
00:00:04,622 --> 00:00:10,481
So a man has only one copy of each X linked gene: he is hemizygous.

3
00:00:10,481 --> 00:00:15,338
A single recessive allele on his one X is enough to show.

4
00:00:15,338 --> 00:00:20,533
That is why red green colour blindness and haemophilia are far commoner in men.

